Explanation:
Article 5 of the 1990 law amends Tax Code Article 238 bis, which is the provision granting a tax deduction for charitable donations. By adding language that expressly includes “payments … to the benefit of a company Foundation,” the amendment confirms that private entities (taxpayers) may claim the deduction when the recipient CSO is of the specified legal type (company foundation).  This satisfies all required ADICO elements: 
• Attribute – private entities (taxpayers);
• Deontic – may (permission inherent in Article 238 bis);
• Aim – take a tax deduction for donations to a qualifying CSO (company foundation);
• Condition – after the law’s commencement; 
• Or-else – optional. 
Therefore the provision is explicitly implemented and the appropriate label is 1.
